# Internal skills (employee-shared)

Copyright (c) 2026 Devrecated.

Skills used **in this repo** by Autodevelop employees that are **not** Autodevelop Brain / subscriber playbooks belong under [`.cursor/skills/autodevelop-internal/`](../../skills/autodevelop-internal/) so the team shares them via git.

## Do

- Put operator / dogfood / meta playbooks under `.cursor/skills/autodevelop-internal/<category>/<name>/SKILL.md`.
- Mirror new leaves under `kits/cursor/skills/autodevelop-internal/` when the kit pack is kept in sync.
- Set `invoke: manual` in `skill-invoke.yaml` for internal skills.
- Keep Brain / sold playbooks in `services/brain/skills/{autodevelop,third-party}/` and wire them through `skill-catalog.yaml` + `bucket_*`.
- Keep client instance bindings under `.cursor/skills/<client-name>/`.

## Do not

- Put those internal skills in `services/brain/skills/` (Brain / hosted product IP).
- Put shared team skills only in `~/.cursor/skills/` (personal machine — invisible to other employees).
- Add internal skills to customer `mcp_buckets.*.may_invoke` or `loops.*.steps`.
- Expose internal skill names as remote MCP tools.
